eczos-windows-core (0.1.1~dev15) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add versioned runner profiles and schema-2 application records.
  * Migrate existing records atomically without recreating their Wine prefixes.
  * Expose safe per-application Wine configuration tools.
  * Add a validated per-application Windows component catalogue.
  * Detect installed Winetricks verbs and record successful installations.
  * Rerun a cached failed EXE or MSI installer in its existing managed prefix.
  * Rediscover the installed executable and restore launchers after retry.
  * Bypass obsolete Flash/Shockwave disc wrappers when a validated Now.ini
    points to the real offline game installer.
  * Recover interrupted installer retries without recreating the prefix.
  * Discover legacy applications registered outside Program Files, including
    App Paths entries that omit the .exe suffix.
  * Resolve registered Windows paths case-insensitively on the Linux host.
  * Ask the user to choose when several credible launch programs remain.
  * Classify legacy DirectPlay applications as games in the application menu.
  * Offer registered launcher/front-end alternatives instead of assuming that
    an App Paths executable is always the user-facing program.
  * Install the archive helpers required by the supported Winetricks workflow.
  * Fetch the pinned Winetricks 20260125 helper with SHA-256 verification so
    Microsoft runtime installs do not rely on Debian's stale download hashes.
  * Support explicit per-application optical mappings with both a mounted disc
    directory and Wine's raw device link for legacy CD checks and CD audio.
  * Accept any verified mountpoint when one optical device is mounted more than
    once instead of checking only the first result returned by findmnt.
  * Remount a configured optical disc through UDisks when an application is
    launched after login, keeping legacy CD mappings usable across restarts.
  * Repair Worms 2's historical C:\\nw2 level and water paths from the managed
    installation and cached original media before launching the game.
  * Launch installed executables from their own application directory instead
    of C:\\, matching Windows and fixing programs that use relative paths.
  * Offer cnc-ddraw as a managed classic-game component for fullscreen scaling
    and matching mouse coordinates in low-resolution DirectDraw games.
  * Configure the Worms 2 profile for fullscreen aspect-preserving scaling and
    scaled mouse coordinates whenever its classic DirectDraw component exists.

 -- EasyComp Zeeland <support@easycompzeeland.nl>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +0200

